Oh, yeah.

746
00:38:06.580 --> 00:38:07.760
He's feeling real good.

747
00:38:08.120 --> 00:38:11.380
And there was a deleted scene, Jenna, that was so good.

748
00:38:11.520 --> 00:38:12.520
He comes in the office.

749
00:38:12.720 --> 00:38:13.840
He's got bagels.

750
00:38:14.000 --> 00:38:15.900
But Pam doesn't have her glasses on.

751
00:38:16.060 --> 00:38:17.620
He tosses a bagel at her.

752
00:38:17.820 --> 00:38:18.920
She can't see it.

753
00:38:19.020 --> 00:38:20.160
It hits her in the face.

754
00:38:20.680 --> 00:38:25.060
And then he goes on, Jenna, to show Pam how to eat a bagel.

755
00:38:25.200 --> 00:38:30.280
He just, with his own hands, starts digging out all the good part of the bagel,

756
00:38:30.280 --> 00:38:31.200
all the middle part.

757
00:38:31.320 --> 00:38:35.140
And he says, yeah, you just eat that outer part, you know, so you don't gain weight.

758
00:38:35.140 --> 00:38:36.700
And he kind of points to Pam's belly.

759
00:38:37.260 --> 00:38:37.460
Yeah.

760
00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:42.240
And I felt like that whole scene showed his state of mind, how manic he is,

761
00:38:42.380 --> 00:38:44.080
throwing the bagels, digging them apart.

762
00:38:44.180 --> 00:38:45.620
Like, oh, my gosh.

763
00:38:45.900 --> 00:38:47.300
I remember shooting that.

764
00:38:47.460 --> 00:38:49.580
I was sad it didn't make it in because that was really fun.

765
00:38:50.000 --> 00:38:51.300
You were so good in it.

766
00:38:51.300 --> 00:38:53.620
I mean, he's like, he tosses a bagel at you.

767
00:38:53.740 --> 00:38:56.220
And Jenna, I really believed you didn't see it.

768
00:38:57.200 --> 00:38:59.020
That's how good you are in the scene.

769
00:38:59.860 --> 00:39:01.560
Anyway, so Ryan is here.

770
00:39:01.640 --> 00:39:03.120
He's actually got some big business.

771
00:39:03.180 --> 00:39:06.660
He goes in the conference room and he calls Jim in.

772
00:39:06.900 --> 00:39:11.920
Toby's there and he's going to give him a formal warning about his job performance.

773
00:39:12.240 --> 00:39:14.860
But the way he calls him in is so amazing.

774
00:39:15.100 --> 00:39:19.680
He's like, hey, Jim, Jim, I got to ask you a question as a true Eagles fan.

775
00:39:19.680 --> 00:39:21.160
Oh, so slimy.

776
00:39:21.540 --> 00:39:24.580
I thought BJ was so good in this scene.

777
00:39:24.760 --> 00:39:27.940
He was like every douchebag I've ever had a meeting with.

778
00:39:28.540 --> 00:39:32.880
I actually recorded it off my computer and I texted it to him.

779
00:39:33.060 --> 00:39:36.300
And I said, BJ, we're watching Did I Stutter?

780
00:39:36.480 --> 00:39:40.060
And you are so brilliant and amazing in the scene.

781
00:39:40.260 --> 00:39:43.220
I just needed you to watch it so you can see how good you are.

782
00:39:44.340 --> 00:39:49.020
And he wrote me back and he was like, Jenna, oh, my God, I forgot about that scene.

783
00:39:49.020 --> 00:39:50.340
Thank you for sending this to me.

784
00:39:50.440 --> 00:39:51.560
That was so fun to watch.

785
00:39:51.740 --> 00:39:54.360
But that happens when we are rewatching this show.

786
00:39:54.740 --> 00:40:00.900
Sometimes I will see one of our friends perform just like madness level amazing.

787
00:40:01.340 --> 00:40:02.660
And I just send it to him.

788
00:40:02.840 --> 00:40:06.600
I'm like, you need to be reminded of what an amazing comedic actor you are.

789
00:40:06.780 --> 00:40:07.420
You're welcome.

790
00:40:07.720 --> 00:40:08.440
Oh, for sure.

791
00:40:08.440 --> 00:40:13.220
I had a whole text thread with Phyllis because I was like, Phyllis, you are so amazing.

792
00:40:13.400 --> 00:40:14.760
Back in Yankee Swap.

793
00:40:15.020 --> 00:40:16.060
She's so good.

794
00:40:16.060 --> 00:40:16.940
I know.

795
00:40:17.640 --> 00:40:18.740
Oh, yes.

796
00:40:18.960 --> 00:40:20.560
BJ is so good in these moments.

797
00:40:20.880 --> 00:40:24.100
And Jim is like, is this because I talked to David Wallace?

798
00:40:24.540 --> 00:40:25.960
And Ryan's like, no, no, no.

799
00:40:26.120 --> 00:40:28.800
I appreciate, you know, constructive criticism.

800
00:40:29.000 --> 00:40:30.040
I thrive on it.

801
00:40:30.220 --> 00:40:30.400
Yeah.

802
00:40:30.620 --> 00:40:31.540
So douchey.

803
00:40:31.920 --> 00:40:34.440
And he says you can get more details from Toby.

804
00:40:34.840 --> 00:40:36.660
This leads to a Toby talking head.

805
00:40:36.840 --> 00:40:39.200
And dare I say that Toby seems smug?

806
00:40:39.580 --> 00:40:40.740
Oh, for sure.

807
00:40:41.320 --> 00:40:41.580
Yeah.

808
00:40:41.900 --> 00:40:47.100
Toby says, I'd say all the goofing around at Pam's desk and hanging out with Pam has finally caught up with him.

809
00:40:47.640 --> 00:40:49.720
Fans were furious, Jenna.

810
00:40:50.100 --> 00:40:53.700
When this episode came out, they hated Toby so much.

811
00:40:53.840 --> 00:40:57.460
I mean, in the episode before, he put his hand on Pam's knee.

812
00:40:57.720 --> 00:40:58.380
Mm-hmm.

813
00:40:58.380 --> 00:41:03.120
And now it seems like he's going behind Jim's back to try to get him fired.

814
00:41:03.480 --> 00:41:03.880
Oh, yeah.

815
00:41:04.420 --> 00:41:11.480
And Jenna, if you thought you hated Toby with that talking head, had you seen the deleted scene between Jim and Toby?

816
00:41:11.780 --> 00:41:14.620
And then Ryan, you would have been like, oh, my God.

817
00:41:14.780 --> 00:41:17.680
People would have, Toby would not have been able to come back from it.

818
00:41:17.840 --> 00:41:19.420
Sam, can you play that deleted scene?

819
00:41:20.080 --> 00:41:21.100
A formal warning.

820
00:41:21.380 --> 00:41:21.600
Seriously.

821
00:41:22.220 --> 00:41:26.440
Well, as you know, Dwight has filed a lot of complaints against you over the years.

822
00:41:26.600 --> 00:41:27.280
And no one cared.

823
00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:30.640
But now it's being looked at as more of a productivity issue.

824
00:41:31.420 --> 00:41:31.900
Productivity?

825
00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:32.800
My numbers are good.

826
00:41:33.080 --> 00:41:33.840
I know.

827
00:41:34.980 --> 00:41:38.140
But Ryan thinks that they're not good enough.

828
00:41:39.180 --> 00:41:40.060
Wallace likes Jim.

829
00:41:40.260 --> 00:41:43.080
So going after him, that's a risky move for me.

830
00:41:43.480 --> 00:41:46.000
But in business, you've got to take risks.

831
00:41:46.480 --> 00:41:50.120
Sometimes you've got to get out on the open highway with a top down.

832
00:41:54.380 --> 00:41:56.440
Oh, my God.

833
00:41:56.860 --> 00:42:00.340
And Ryan is trying to put the top down to his car and it won't go down.

834
00:42:01.840 --> 00:42:02.360
Wow.

835
00:42:02.820 --> 00:42:05.500
But, yeah, can you imagine if those scenes have been left in?

836
00:42:06.260 --> 00:42:16.160
Oh, well, Angela, speaking of treachery, Dwight has washed the Xterra and he's now reselling it for over $9,000.

837
00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:18.560
He's selling it for a profit.

838
00:42:18.960 --> 00:42:21.460
Oh, and Andy is like, what the hell, man?

839
00:42:22.360 --> 00:42:23.320
Angela's impressed.

840
00:42:24.080 --> 00:42:25.260
Angela's like, oh, yeah.

841
00:42:25.680 --> 00:42:26.020
Mm-hmm.

842
00:42:26.560 --> 00:42:27.280
You got him.

843
00:42:27.380 --> 00:42:28.000
You're smarter.

844
00:42:28.460 --> 00:42:30.580
She loves two men dueling over her.

845
00:42:30.860 --> 00:42:31.840
She really does.

846
00:42:32.040 --> 00:42:32.400
I know.

847
00:42:32.880 --> 00:42:35.600
You guys remember, Michael has run out of options.

848
00:42:35.860 --> 00:42:37.580
Fluffy fingers isn't going to work for him.

849
00:42:38.280 --> 00:42:40.940
So he's going to have to do the thing he didn't want to do.

850
00:42:41.200 --> 00:42:44.700
He's going to have to fake fire Stanley to teach him a lesson.

851
00:42:44.700 --> 00:42:48.480
And he comes out of his office and he announces it to everyone.

852
00:42:48.660 --> 00:42:55.020
He says, guys, guys, guys, listen, I'm going to fake fire Stanley, but I just want you to react as if I'm really firing Stanley.

853
00:42:55.280 --> 00:43:00.840
And everybody's like, if you hadn't told us what you were doing, we would have reacted correctly.

854
00:43:01.440 --> 00:43:04.400
And he's like, oh, my gosh, why aren't you understanding this?

855
00:43:04.400 --> 00:43:08.780
The person that says it, the person that's the voice of reason is Kevin.

856
00:43:09.440 --> 00:43:10.420
I know.

857
00:43:10.740 --> 00:43:14.360
You know you're in trouble when Kevin is the voice of reason.

858
00:43:14.920 --> 00:43:18.780
Stanley walks into the bullpen and Michael fake fires him.

859
00:43:18.940 --> 00:43:21.140
And it does not go well.

860
00:43:21.360 --> 00:43:23.960
Stanley unleashes on him.

861
00:43:24.140 --> 00:43:27.600
Just a tirade of insults.

862
00:43:27.840 --> 00:43:31.800
I remember when we filmed this, Jenna, and you could have heard a pin drop.

863
00:43:32.200 --> 00:43:32.700
Yes.

864
00:43:32.700 --> 00:43:36.480
It was such a beautifully dramatic moment.

865
00:43:37.920 --> 00:43:39.660
Leslie crushed it.

866
00:43:39.940 --> 00:43:44.380
Yeah, you guys, we reached out to Leslie because we really,

867
00:43:44.640 --> 00:43:52.660
really wanted him to come on the pod today because this is just a tour de force storyline and performance by him in this episode.

868
00:43:52.920 --> 00:43:55.740
And he is filming this week.

869
00:43:55.920 --> 00:43:59.220
He is filming something and he couldn't come on.

870
00:43:59.220 --> 00:44:02.740
But he did want us to share with you that this monologue was completely scripted.

871
00:44:02.900 --> 00:44:04.020
This was not improvised.

872
00:44:04.240 --> 00:44:11.760
You know, and I remember, Angela, that he worked on this and he delivered it like it was just an amazing performance.

873
00:44:11.760 --> 00:44:13.300
And he nailed it every take.

874
00:44:13.460 --> 00:44:14.060
Every take.

875
00:44:14.060 --> 00:44:16.160
He was 100% off book.

876
00:44:16.300 --> 00:44:18.300
He showed up ready to throw it down.

877
00:44:18.560 --> 00:44:22.420
And we were just all so happy for him.

878
00:44:22.780 --> 00:44:24.100
This moment was amazing.

879
00:44:24.100 --> 00:44:26.740
And I remember us all applauding at the end of the scene.

880
00:44:26.940 --> 00:44:27.340
Yeah.

881
00:44:27.520 --> 00:44:29.160
Well, Michael throws everybody out.

882
00:44:29.920 --> 00:44:32.220
He yells and says, everybody get out.

883
00:44:32.420 --> 00:44:32.800
Everybody.

884
00:44:32.980 --> 00:44:33.620
Except Stanley.

885
00:44:33.880 --> 00:44:34.500
Everybody out.

886
00:44:34.720 --> 00:44:36.840
And everyone gets the hell out.

887
00:44:37.040 --> 00:44:47.260
And Jenna, in the script, which isn't in the deleted scenes, but in the script, Michael turns to the cameras and says, you two cameras out of here.

888
00:44:47.500 --> 00:44:48.020
Everybody.

889
00:44:48.740 --> 00:44:49.060
Wow.

890
00:44:49.360 --> 00:44:55.600
And that's why at 18 minutes, 17 seconds, you see the cameras sneak back in.

891
00:44:55.740 --> 00:44:58.820
It's because in the script, Michael told them to get out.

892
00:44:59.320 --> 00:45:00.580
I loved that move.

893
00:45:01.020 --> 00:45:09.240
I loved it because when Michael is alone with Stanley or thinks he's alone with Stanley, he gets really vulnerable.

894
00:45:09.480 --> 00:45:10.800
There's tears in his eyes.

895
00:45:10.800 --> 00:45:13.640
And he says, why do you pick on me?

896
00:45:13.940 --> 00:45:16.200
Like, why do you pick on me like this?

897
00:45:16.360 --> 00:45:17.740
And it's really vulnerable.

898
00:45:18.560 --> 00:45:21.980
And Stanley, very matter-of-factly, says, I don't respect you.

899
00:45:22.600 --> 00:45:31.360
And then I felt like Michael had such an honest moment that could not have happened if the cameras were there, where he says, fine, I accept that.

900
00:45:31.620 --> 00:45:32.700
You don't respect me.

901
00:45:32.820 --> 00:45:33.960
I accept it.

902
00:45:34.040 --> 00:45:37.320
But you can't talk to me like that here.

903
00:45:37.760 --> 00:45:39.180
I am your boss.

904
00:45:39.360 --> 00:45:41.180
And it just cannot be done.

905
00:45:41.180 --> 00:45:43.240
And I agree with you, Angela.

906
00:45:43.600 --> 00:45:50.560
Anytime Michael knows the cameras are there, he can't help but perform in some way for them.

907
00:45:51.110 --> 00:45:57.860
And so I feel like we're seeing a side of Michael Scott that can only be seen when he doesn't know the cameras are there.

908
00:45:58.540 --> 00:45:58.680
Yeah.

909
00:45:58.680 --> 00:46:06.200
And that was such a fun part of our show, playing with who are our characters when we know the cameras are there and when we don't.

910
00:46:06.340 --> 00:46:11.600
And I loved that we got to reveal these little different parts of ourselves in these different ways.

911
00:46:12.100 --> 00:46:12.960
Oh, me too.

912
00:46:13.120 --> 00:46:15.120
It made the show so rich, right?

913
00:46:15.400 --> 00:46:16.040
It's cool.

914
00:46:16.220 --> 00:46:16.960
And you know what?

915
00:46:17.080 --> 00:46:18.480
They have this moment of resolution.

916
00:46:18.880 --> 00:46:19.740
They're like, fine.

917
00:46:19.740 --> 00:46:22.180
We now know our rules of engagement, right?

918
00:46:22.180 --> 00:46:23.640
Yeah, they shake hands.

919
00:46:24.140 --> 00:46:24.280
Done.

920
00:46:24.560 --> 00:46:27.260
This leads to Michael having a talking head.

921
00:46:27.400 --> 00:46:32.520
He's really stuck on the idea of respect, getting no respect.

922
00:46:32.600 --> 00:46:36.620
And this just sends his brain into Rodney Dangerfield land.

923
00:46:36.920 --> 00:46:43.180
So he's going to do some real kind of like off-the-cuff Rodney Dangerfield impressions,

924
00:46:43.180 --> 00:46:51.220
which morphs into a Jeff Foxworthy impression and then Borat and then Jerry Seinfeld and then back to Rodney Dangerfield again.

925
00:46:51.220 --> 00:46:53.360
And it's a pretty epic talking head.

926
00:46:53.660 --> 00:46:54.600
It is.

927
00:46:54.780 --> 00:47:02.020
Well, you know, Jenna, that talking head, that whole Rodney Dangerfield comic riff is not in the shooting draft.

928
00:47:02.200 --> 00:47:03.320
It's a whole other talking head.

929
00:47:03.520 --> 00:47:03.800
Huh.

930
00:47:04.060 --> 00:47:06.940
So I have to imagine they handed Steve a whole bunch of alts.

931
00:47:07.060 --> 00:47:08.180
They would do that to us, right?

932
00:47:08.620 --> 00:47:12.200
And this is the one that they picked because that is not the one in the script.

933
00:47:13.200 --> 00:47:13.600
Interesting.

934
00:47:13.980 --> 00:47:15.180
Well, I liked this one.

935
00:47:15.360 --> 00:47:15.960
I did too.

936
00:47:16.140 --> 00:47:18.640
And I have to think Steve improvised a little.

937
00:47:18.800 --> 00:47:19.720
I think it was on the page.

938
00:47:19.720 --> 00:47:21.980
But I can sort of see Steve doing his thing.

939
00:47:22.320 --> 00:47:23.080
I'm sure.

940
00:47:23.560 --> 00:47:28.040
While that talking head was happening, everyone else is in the parking lot, you know?

941
00:47:28.280 --> 00:47:29.380
They're heading home.

942
00:47:29.780 --> 00:47:35.040
There is a wrap-up scene of the Dwight, Andy, Angela love triangle.

943
00:47:35.560 --> 00:47:39.700
It's in the shooting draft, and it didn't make it to the deleted scenes.

944
00:47:39.920 --> 00:47:41.740
But Andy and Angela walk to the car.

945
00:47:41.740 --> 00:47:48.200
They pass by Dwight, who is scraping off a Cornell sticker from the back window of the Xterra.

946
00:47:48.580 --> 00:47:50.640
And Andy says, goodbye, old friend.

947
00:47:50.880 --> 00:47:54.640
May all your roads be downhill and the wind be on your back windshield.

948
00:47:54.920 --> 00:47:56.680
And Angela's like, Andy.

949
00:47:57.220 --> 00:48:00.040
And Andy says, I can't believe Dwight would do me like that.

950
00:48:00.180 --> 00:48:01.820
He took advantage of my kindness.

951
00:48:02.140 --> 00:48:05.060
And Angela says, he didn't take advantage of you.

952
00:48:05.220 --> 00:48:06.200
He bested you.

953
00:48:11.980 --> 00:48:15.580
And she looks at Dwight like he's super hot.

954
00:48:16.900 --> 00:48:17.540
Yeah.

955
00:48:17.920 --> 00:48:22.940
Well, Angela, we should just call these deleted scenes feisty in the parking lot.

956
00:48:22.940 --> 00:48:29.580
Because I know that over by Pam and Jim's car, there is a scene that we shot that I believe

957
00:48:29.580 --> 00:48:36.880
is in the deleted scenes where Jim tells Pam the truth about Ryan and what Ryan said to him

958
00:48:36.880 --> 00:48:40.460
and that he's gunning for him to maybe get fired or put him on notice.

959
00:48:40.680 --> 00:48:42.860
And Pam is not having it.

960
00:48:43.020 --> 00:48:45.260
Oh, I titled it Pam's Pissed.

961
00:48:45.420 --> 00:48:45.900
Yeah.

962
00:48:46.180 --> 00:48:48.060
And Sam, you got to play that clip.

963
00:48:49.780 --> 00:48:51.260
Hey, what really happened today?

964
00:48:51.540 --> 00:48:51.920
What do you mean?

965
00:48:52.160 --> 00:48:55.060
I mean, I don't need my glasses to know when something's stressing you out.

966
00:48:55.220 --> 00:48:55.760
What happened today?

967
00:48:58.460 --> 00:48:59.920
Ryan is trying to get rid of me.

968
00:49:01.160 --> 00:49:04.640
He came in today to give me an official warning about my job performance.

969
00:49:05.080 --> 00:49:05.400
What?

970
00:49:06.720 --> 00:49:08.260
God, he's such a creep.

971
00:49:09.240 --> 00:49:10.800
That really pisses me off.

972
00:49:11.420 --> 00:49:12.740
I'm going to bash his face in.

973
00:49:12.880 --> 00:49:14.740
I'm going to bash his face in with a stale bagel.

974
00:49:14.940 --> 00:49:16.220
Then I'm going to throw a rock at his car.

975
00:49:17.220 --> 00:49:18.780
Come on, we're going to New York right now.

976
00:49:18.840 --> 00:49:19.240
I'm driving.

977
00:49:19.360 --> 00:49:21.180
If I hit him without my glasses, I don't think it's a crime.

978
00:49:21.740 --> 00:49:22.060
Great.

979
00:49:23.180 --> 00:49:25.200
God, I should have told you all about this sooner.

980
00:49:25.680 --> 00:49:26.520
What a jerk.

981
00:49:26.760 --> 00:49:27.720
What a jerk.

982
00:49:29.200 --> 00:49:36.740
Can you imagine if they had left in the sex talk between Jim and Pam up at the top and

983
00:49:36.740 --> 00:49:41.760
then this scene of Pam saying she's going to throw a rock at Ryan or maybe hit him with

984
00:49:41.760 --> 00:49:42.380
her car?

985
00:49:42.840 --> 00:49:44.100
Oh, my gosh.

986
00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:46.720
And in the shooting draft, it was much shorter.

987
00:49:46.720 --> 00:49:48.760
You just said, I'm going to smash his face.

988
00:49:48.760 --> 00:49:50.600
And that was it, you know.

989
00:49:50.740 --> 00:49:54.000
But in this deleted scene, Pam is going off.

990
00:49:54.260 --> 00:49:55.680
You do not mess with her, man.

991
00:49:56.000 --> 00:49:56.980
I guess not.

992
